Subject: [PATCH] recover zero child IDs, resolving ambiguous threads at clone exit

Use a unique procfs match for delivered creation events with a zero child
PID. When concurrent thread clones are ambiguous, keep the creator's real
flags and obtain its exact child TID from the clone syscall return value.
Validate that TID against the traced thread group before existing child setup.
Do not defer vfork, guess parents, or select by PID order. Missing creation
events and ambiguous process (non-thread) clones remain unsupported.
No timers or polling are added by this recovery patch.

